---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="IRB & Ethics FAQ | Rex Autistikōn Labs"
  description="Information for institutional review boards and ethics committees regarding data handling on the Rex Autistikōn Labs research platform."
>
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">IRB &amp; Ethics FAQ</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Information for institutional review boards, ethics committees, and site investigators
        evaluating use of the Rex Autistikōn Labs research platform.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">What is the platform?</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            A secure research tool operated by Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc., a U.S. 501(c)(3)
            public charity. Approved collaborators submit coded measurement data for server-side
            Kelvin–Voigt and free-energy calculations. The platform is not a diagnostic device and is
            not a clinical service.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">What data are stored?</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-slate-600 space-y-2">
            <li>Collaborator identity (institutional email / lab ID via Microsoft Entra sign-in)</li>
            <li>Optional study or protocol ID and session number</li>
            <li>Participant pseudonym (direct identifiers are not required by the platform)</li>
            <li>Research classification fields as provided by the collaborator (e.g., group, age, region)</li>
            <li>Zone measurement parameters and computed outputs (fidelity, π_eff, free energy, MPA)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Who can see individual records?</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-slate-600 space-y-2">
            <li>The submitting collaborator sees full detail of their own results.</li>
            <li>Foundation administrators may access records for system integrity and approved operations.</li>
            <li>Other collaborators see only de-identified aggregates (no individual lab identity; no single-source raw data from other sites).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Where are data stored?</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Microsoft Azure (United States region). Authentication uses Microsoft Entra ID.
            Intake and results pages require sign-in. Data are stored in Azure Cosmos DB under the
            Foundation’s subscription.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Who is responsible for ethics approval?</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The collaborating institution. Local IRB or ethics approval and informed consent
            (where required) remain the responsibility of the site investigator. The Foundation
            does not replace institutional review and does not claim oversight of local human-subjects protocols.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Is data shared externally?</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Not without explicit written agreement. Aggregate, de-identified summaries may be used
            for scientific reporting consistent with the access model above.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Contact</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Technical or data-security questions:
            <a href="mailto:info@rexautistikonlabs.org" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">
              info@rexautistikonlabs.org
            </a><br />
            <a href="https://rexautistikonlabs.org" class="text-teal-700 font-medium hover:text-teal-800">
              rexautistikonlabs.org
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 mt-10">
        This FAQ is informational and does not constitute legal advice. Institutions should apply
        their own policies and counsel as appropriate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
